#############################################################################################################

[+] VIRTUALIZATION STACK

+] VIRTUALIZATION STACK

├── KVM
│   └── Hardware virtualization module built into the Linux kernel.
│       Uses Intel VT-x or AMD-V to accelerate virtual machines.
│
├── QEMU
│   ├── Emulator and virtual machine monitor.
│   ├── Uses KVM for near-native performance when available.
│   ├── qemu-system-x86
│   │   └── Runs x86/x86_64 virtual machines.
│   └── qemu-utils
│       └── Utilities such as qemu-img, qemu-nbd, and qemu-io.
│
├── libvirt
│   ├── Virtualization management API and daemon.
│   ├── libvirt-daemon-system
│   │   └── Installs and configures the libvirt daemon.
│   └── libvirt-clients
│       └── Command-line tools such as virsh and virt-install.
│
└── virt-manager
    └── Graphical interface for creating and managing virtual machines through libvirt.

$ sudo apt install -y qemu-system-x86 qemu-utils libvirt-daemon-system libvirt-clients virt-manager

$ sudo systemctl enable --now libvirtd

$ systemctl status libvirtd

$ sudo usermod -aG libvirt,kvm $USER

- Verify the groups that you are in, you should see both: libvirt and kvm

$ groups
